# Normalize line endings. Text files are stored with LF in the repo and
# checked out with the platform-native ending, so the LF->CRLF warnings stop.
* text=auto

# Windows-only scripts should keep CRLF on checkout.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Shell scripts should stay LF everywhere.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Frozen raw source snapshots: store exact bytes, never normalize line endings,
# so the SHA-256 hashes recorded in data/raw/source_manifest.json stay valid on
# any checkout (reproducibility requirement of the build spec).
data/raw/** -text

# Treat common binary assets as binary (never normalized).
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
*.parquet binary
*.npy binary
*.npz binary
# Append-only session logs (INSTRUCTIONS.md section 3) that grow without bound
# every session. Marked -diff so git diff renders them as
# "Binary files a/CONVERSATION_LOG.md and b/CONVERSATION_LOG.md differ"
# instead of the full content. The files stay fully tracked and human-readable
# in the working tree; only the diff representation changes. Without this,
# every worker commit's diff would include the whole session's turn-by-turn
# capture and blow the reviewer's context budget (measured 2026-09-03: iter2
# review at 462k tokens against a 200k limit, driven almost entirely by an
# 11,563-line append to CONVERSATION_LOG.md).
CONVERSATION_LOG.md -diff
LABNOTEBOOK.md -diff
